        "parms": "# stripnote — note-ons only\nstripnote passes a note only when its velocity is not 0. Every note source reports a release as velocity 0, so a patch that should act once per key, such as starting a sound or counting notes, acts twice without it. The right inlet stores a velocity and sends nothing; a pitch on the left inlet goes out with that velocity, velocity first, unless the velocity is 0. A list <pitch> <velocity> sets the velocity, then tests the pitch.\nIt works as Max's stripnote does. Nothing is clamped: any velocity other than 0 passes.",
